-- emit: the derived `compare` of a STRUCTURAL shape — a record, a tuple,
-- `()` (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §9.2, §9.3, §8.5, A.46).
--
-- The `eq` half is `emit/DerivedEqShapes.beni`; this is what the other
-- half looks like, and the difference is not cosmetic. `eq` conjoins its
-- positions and is one expression; `compare` is LEXICOGRAPHIC, so every
-- position but the last is bound to a `const` and returned early unless it
-- is `"EQ"`. Fields go in name-text order, which is the order the object's
-- keys are already in (§4); tuple slots go `a`, `b`, `c`.
--
-- **The golden is §9's SHAPE, not its listing.** §9.2 names the
-- intermediates `o0`, `o1` and braces each block; the emitter writes
-- `$o$0`, `$o$1` and numbers them per FUNCTION rather than per block,
-- because the printer gives a `switch` arm no braces of its own and two
-- arms of one `switch` share a block scope. The structure is the spec's;
-- the spelling is this file's.
--
-- Four things to read here:
--
--   - one function per shape, keyed on the shape alone — `( Int, Int )`
--     and `( Char, Float )` share `compare$t2` and differ only in the
--     evidence each use hands it (A.46);
--   - `compare$unit` answers `"EQ"` and takes no evidence: `()` is `null`
--     at runtime and both operands hold the same value;
--   - a `String` position takes `String$compare` — the core function, a
--     CALL and never `<` — and a `Char` one takes `compare$char`, the
--     code-point comparator of §9.1: the two rows of §3.2 JavaScript's
--     `<` gets wrong, and both are FUNCTIONS here because every position
--     of a structural shape is answered by the evidence a use hands it
--     (the inline operators are `emit/DerivedCompareNominal.beni`);
--   - `rank` puts the record's comparator in VALUE position, so it is the
--     eta-expansion of §8.2 and not the bare name: `compare$r$x$y` is a
--     function of four arguments and the evidence slot promised one of
--     two.
--
-- The `$order` pass of §8.5 is empty here: no shape has tags.
import Node exposing (Program)
import String


pub before : { x : Int, y : String }, { x : Int, y : String } -> Bool
before a b =
    a < b


pub atLeast : { x : Int, y : String }, { x : Int, y : String } -> Bool
atLeast a b =
    a >= b


pub pairAtMost : ( Int, Int ), ( Int, Int ) -> Bool
pairAtMost a b =
    a <= b


pub mixedAfter : ( Char, Float ), ( Char, Float ) -> Bool
mixedAfter a b =
    a > b


pub tripleBefore : ( Int, Char, String ), ( Int, Char, String ) -> Bool
tripleBefore a b =
    a < b


pub unitAtMost : (), () -> Bool
unitAtMost a b =
    a <= b


order : a, a -> Order
    where a.compare : a, a -> Order
order x y =
    x.compare y


pub rank : { x : Int, y : String } -> Order
rank r =
    order r r


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines []
